WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:04.771
The U.S. National Library of
Medicine presents

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.139
"Mercury and Our Health,"

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.240
A short film by the

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.642
Environmental Health
Student Portal

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:27.794
[Paul] Hi mom, thanks again for the sushi! I'll watch a little

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.429
bit of TV while I
am eating, and then

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.264
I am going to go do my homework.

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:34.033
[Mom] Ok, but don't
watch it for too long!

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:36.469
[From T.V.]
This is Kate,

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.638
from "Food Science
for Consumers."

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:41.508
Today's episode is about
mercury in seafood.

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:44.911
There may be too much mercury in the seafood you are eating.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:48.114
Watch to find out, and learn how to protect your health!

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:53.586
[Paul] Mercury in seafood? I wonder... Is the sushi seafood?

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:58.057
[Kate] It sure is, but don't be alarmed before you learn more!

00:00:58.057 --> 00:01:01.628
[Paul] Mom! The T.V. characters are coming to life again!

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:03.163
[Mom] That's nice, dear.

00:01:03.163 --> 00:01:04.898
[Kate] Do you know
what mercury is?

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:08.735
[Paul] No, but it sounds like
it's something bad.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.470
[Kate] Mercury is a
natural metal that's

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.106
found in the air,
water and soil.

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:15.074
[Paul] What do you
mean by natural?

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.510
[Kate] Natural means it's a
part of the environment,

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.312
and is not made by humans.

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:22.182
It also exists in
the Earth's crust.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:25.218
[Paul] Wait! What do
you mean by crust?

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:33.293
Cool!

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:34.694
[Kate] The crust
is the outermost

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.596
rocky layer of the planet.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:41.334
[Paul] Whoa! Cool! Where are we?

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:44.170
[Kate] We are on the
periodic table of elements.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.939
You see, we can find
mercury on this

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:49.442
table of elements by looking over its chemical symbol.

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.711
[Paul] What's the chemical
symbol of mercury?

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:54.714
[Kate] The chemical
symbol of mercury is Hg.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:57.550
This is how we can find it
on the periodic table.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.554
Remember that we
can find mercury

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:04.424
in the environment
in several forms.

00:02:04.424 --> 00:02:07.126
Sometimes, atoms of
mercury exist alone,

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:08.962
not connected
with other elements.

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:13.366
This form of mercury is called metallic, or elemental.

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:16.135
People also call this
kind of mercury "quicksilver"

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:17.403
or "liquid mercury"

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.205
because it's
a shiny, silver liquid

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:22.008
that can evaporate
into an invisible gas.

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:23.209
[Paul] Oh, I see.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.411
[Kate] At other times,
atoms of mercury combine with

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:28.848
other elements and create compounds, or chemical mixtures.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.351
We may encounter mercury
in different situations

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.786
depending on
what form it is in.

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:37.223
Different forms of mercury also affect our health differently.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.325
[Paul] How can mercury
affect my health?

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.699
[Kate] If enough mercury
gets into your body,

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.568
it could really make you sick.

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:51.738
[Paul] Oh, I don't
like being sick!

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.239
[Kate] Of course you don't!

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.846
Luckily, if you live in the U.S., there are not that many

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:02.815
ways for you to have contact
with a lot of mercury.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:05.818
[Paul] But, what
exactly does mercury do?

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.287
[Kate] Well, that depends.

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:08.388
[Paul] Depends on what?

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:09.689
[Kate] Several things!

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:12.125
Like, how much mercury
gets into your body,

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:14.427
the form of mercury
that gets into your body,

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.496
how the mercury
gets into your body,

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:19.032
and how long you're
exposed to mercury.

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:23.603
High levels of
mercury in the body

00:03:23.603 --> 00:03:26.239
can really hurt
many body systems,

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:28.608
especially the
brain and kidneys.

00:03:28.608 --> 00:03:31.177
[Paul] The brain? How
does it hurt the brain?

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.412
[Kate] These are
some of the symptoms of

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:34.614
brain damage from
mercury poisoning.

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:37.083
Tremors, or
trembling and shaking, and

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.618
not being able to stop.

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:41.321
Walking impairments,
or having difficulty walking.

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:44.390
Speech impairments, or having difficulty forming clear words.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.125
Changes in vision or hearing.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.093
Memory loss.

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:49.495
Loss of appetite,
or not feeling hungry.

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:51.764
Feeling
irritated, and psychosis,

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:54.701
or losing touch with reality, such as seeing or hearing

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:56.336
things that
are not there.

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:57.437
[Paul]
I don't like it.

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:59.072
Can it do this to anyone?

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:02.308
[Kate] Yes, mercury poisoning
could happen to anyone,

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:06.145
but it is especially damaging
to children and unborn babies.

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:11.217
[Paul] But I am a child! Why is it especially bad for children?

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:14.053
[Kate] Because their nervous systems are still developing.

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:16.456
The younger the child
is, the more sensitive

00:04:16.456 --> 00:04:18.725
he or she is to mercury.

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:20.827
You are more
sensitive than an adult,

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:22.295
but young
children and babies

00:04:22.295 --> 00:04:24.597
are even more
sensitive than you are.

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:26.899
[Paul] But you said that there are not that many ways for me to

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.135
have contact with
a lot of mercury.

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:30.903
I guess that's
the good news.

00:04:30.903 --> 00:04:32.171
But then you also
said that mercury

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:34.240
is a natural
part of the Earth.

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.809
This makes the Earth
a dangerous place!

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:44.684
[Kate] Mercury can only hurt us if we come in contact with it -

00:04:44.684 --> 00:04:46.919
touch it, breathe
it, and swallow it.

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:49.622
Mercury in the Earth's
crust is hidden in the rocks.

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:51.858
So, the amount of mercury
that's normally found in the

00:04:51.858 --> 00:04:55.828
environment is very,
very small and will not hurt us.

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:57.363
[Paul] That's good to hear.

00:04:57.363 --> 00:05:00.633
[Kate] Yes. Unfortunately, people do things that make

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:03.803
mercury come out where we can come in contact with it.

00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:05.171
[Paul] What do you
mean, people do things

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:06.806
that make mercury come out?

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.341
[Kate] Let me
give you an example.

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:12.245
I mentioned that mercury
is found in many rocks,

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:13.513
including coal.

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.815
People burn coal for energy.

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:19.152
Unfortunately, when we burn coal, we release its mercury

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:21.421
into the air
and the environment.

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:22.722
[Paul] Oh, I see.

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:29.762
[Kate] Mercury
also has many properties that

00:05:29.762 --> 00:05:33.499
people find useful, so we
use it in commercial products.

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.368
[Paul] What kinds of properties?

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:37.804
[Kate] For example,
pure, or elemental,

00:05:37.804 --> 00:05:39.906
mercury conducts electricity.

00:05:39.906 --> 00:05:41.774
It also combines
with other metals,

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:43.876
into combinations
that have many uses.

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:46.345
Other forms of
mercury kill bacteria.

00:05:46.345 --> 00:05:49.782
So, we use mercury
in some commercial products.

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:51.050
[Paul] I am not
sure I like this.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:53.553
We use
mercury in products?

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:56.022
[Kate] Yes, but
less than we used to.

00:05:56.022 --> 00:05:57.523
People have known
about the helpful,

00:05:57.523 --> 00:06:00.727
useful characteristics of mercury for a long time.

00:06:00.727 --> 00:06:02.962
but the knowledge about
its dangers to human health

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.197
is more recent.

00:06:04.197 --> 00:06:07.667
In the past, people often
used mercury in medicines,

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:09.969
because of its
bacteria-killing properties.

00:06:09.969 --> 00:06:11.971
[Paul] Oh,
that's ironic.

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:13.906
[Kate] But in general,
now that we know that

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:15.508
mercury can
be dangerous,

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:18.511
we look for alternatives
to it whenever we can.

00:06:18.511 --> 00:06:20.947
[Paul] So, what
products have mercury?

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:23.649
[Kate] Let me give
you some examples:

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:24.884
Glass thermometers

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:26.419
Electrical switches

00:06:26.419 --> 00:06:29.355
Fluorescent light bulbs

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:31.290
Dental fillings

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.760
Vaccine preservatives

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:36.162
Some medical equipment

00:06:36.162 --> 00:06:38.131
Some batteries

00:06:38.131 --> 00:06:39.398
And old paints.

00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:42.235
[Paul] Wait! There's
mercury in thermometers?

00:06:42.235 --> 00:06:44.137
[Kate] In some
glass thermometers.

00:06:44.137 --> 00:06:47.740
Heat makes mercury expand, or grow, and this property of

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:50.977
mercury was used in
mercury-in-glass thermometers.

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:53.746
These thermometers
were used for centuries.

00:06:53.746 --> 00:06:56.048
But now that we know that mercury can be dangerous,

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:57.383
they have become rare.

00:06:57.383 --> 00:07:00.019
[Paul] I've seen them in pictures, inside books.

00:07:00.019 --> 00:07:00.887
[Kate] That's right.

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:04.190
But the thermometer your parents use to take your temperature

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:06.225
probably looks
like this and uses

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:08.394
an electronic
temperature sensor.

00:07:08.394 --> 00:07:09.462
[Paul] Did people
get hurt a lot

00:07:09.462 --> 00:07:11.898
by all those old
glass thermometers?

00:07:11.898 --> 00:07:14.100
[Kate] Remember,
mercury is dangerous to us

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:17.370
only when we touch
it, breathe it, or swallow it.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:19.205
We cannot touch,
breathe, or swallow

00:07:19.205 --> 00:07:21.073
mercury inside a thermometer.

00:07:21.073 --> 00:07:23.209
The danger happens
when someone accidentally

00:07:23.209 --> 00:07:25.077
breaks the thermometer.

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:29.248
[Paul] Glass things are easy to break! What happened then?

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:32.552
[Kate] Well, the shiny, silver elemental mercury would spill

00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:37.056
and collect into silver balls - beautiful, but dangerous.

00:07:37.056 --> 00:07:40.393
Someone cleaning up the spill could accidentally touch it.

00:07:40.393 --> 00:07:42.128
Look how
dangerous that is!

00:07:44.197 --> 00:07:46.332
There was also risk
of breathing it, because

00:07:46.332 --> 00:07:50.369
liquid elemental mercury evaporated into invisible gas.

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:51.704
[Paul] What about batteries?

00:07:51.704 --> 00:07:54.240
[Kate] For a long time,
companies around the world used

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:57.276
mercury to make
many kinds of batteries.

00:07:57.276 --> 00:07:59.712
They did it because mercury prevented the buildup of

00:07:59.712 --> 00:08:01.614
hydrogen gas
in batteries, which can

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:04.650
cause the battery
to bulge and leak.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:07.353
Since the 1980s, the use
of mercury in batteries

00:08:07.353 --> 00:08:09.789
in the U.S. has
been going down.

00:08:09.789 --> 00:08:12.158
[Paul] What about the
batteries in my TV remote?

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:13.826
Do they have mercury?

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:15.895
[Kate] Most batteries
made in the U.S. today

00:08:15.895 --> 00:08:19.232
do not have mercury
in them, with few exceptions.

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:22.802
Your typical AA or AAA batteries
for your remote control

00:08:22.802 --> 00:08:24.770
do not have
mercury in them.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.038
[Paul] Oh,
that's good.

00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:28.140
But, which
batteries have it then?

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:31.277
[Kate] One of the exceptions
is button cell batteries.

00:08:31.277 --> 00:08:33.646
These are very small
batteries that look like

00:08:33.646 --> 00:08:36.015
coins or buttons
and are used in

00:08:36.015 --> 00:08:39.652
small portable electronic devices, like wrist watches.

00:08:39.652 --> 00:08:42.421
[Paul] Oh, my watch
has a battery like that!

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:43.823
Should I get rid of it?

00:08:43.823 --> 00:08:46.259
[Kate] Remember, mercury
can only hurt you if you

00:08:46.259 --> 00:08:48.694
touch it, breathe
it, or swallow it.

00:08:48.694 --> 00:08:50.396
You aren't touching
the mercury, because it's

00:08:50.396 --> 00:08:53.032
inside the battery
inside the watch.

00:08:53.032 --> 00:08:55.368
[Paul] But you said
dental fillings have mercury!

00:08:55.368 --> 00:08:57.770
Those definitely
go inside our bodies.

00:08:57.770 --> 00:09:00.439
[Kate] Have you ever
heard of "silver fillings"?

00:09:00.439 --> 00:09:03.442
They're called silver
because of their silver color,

00:09:03.442 --> 00:09:05.878
but they are actually
an amalgam, or blend

00:09:05.878 --> 00:09:09.181
of metallic mercury,
silver, and some other metals.

00:09:09.181 --> 00:09:11.918
Very small amounts
of mercury are slowly released

00:09:11.918 --> 00:09:13.819
from the
blend over time.

00:09:13.819 --> 00:09:16.122
For example, while you chew!

00:09:16.122 --> 00:09:18.057
[Paul] See? I knew it!

00:09:18.057 --> 00:09:20.493
[Kate] But you have to remember that the amount makes a big

00:09:20.493 --> 00:09:23.396
difference in whether
something is dangerous or not.

00:09:23.396 --> 00:09:26.399
From what we know right
now, amalgam dental fillings

00:09:26.399 --> 00:09:29.035
do not harm people's health.

00:09:29.035 --> 00:09:31.771
[Paul] I don't get it. It sounds like a lot of these products

00:09:31.771 --> 00:09:33.673
that have mercury in
them keep it hidden

00:09:33.673 --> 00:09:35.942
or put in very small amounts.

00:09:35.942 --> 00:09:38.678
So, does this mean that we have nothing to worry about?

00:09:38.678 --> 00:09:39.946
[Kate] Not really.

00:09:39.946 --> 00:09:42.214
Remember, a lot
of the products I mentioned

00:09:42.214 --> 00:09:44.684
eventually break
or become useless,

00:09:44.684 --> 00:09:47.019
so we'll need to get
rid of them at some point.

00:09:47.019 --> 00:09:49.989
[Paul] You mean, throw them in the trash! That's easy!

00:09:49.989 --> 00:09:51.691
[Kate] It's not that simple.

00:09:54.694 --> 00:09:57.863
[Paul] Ewww! Gross! It stinks!

00:09:57.863 --> 00:09:59.165
[Kate] If we
simply dump trash

00:09:59.165 --> 00:10:01.634
that has mercury in
it into the environment,

00:10:01.634 --> 00:10:05.137
it will go into our soil and water, and build up there.

00:10:05.137 --> 00:10:06.739
[Paul] So, what
are we supposed to do

00:10:06.739 --> 00:10:09.075
with the mercury
containing products?

00:10:09.075 --> 00:10:11.410
We can't keep the
broken stuff forever!

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:14.680
[Kate] We have special ways
to get rid of mercury waste.

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.449
Many cities and
towns now have

00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:19.585
hazardous household
waste facilities or events,

00:10:19.585 --> 00:10:22.455
but many products that
have mercury still end up in

00:10:22.455 --> 00:10:25.424
landfills or
incinerators that burn trash.

00:10:25.424 --> 00:10:28.260
Which means mercury
is eventually released

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:31.964
into the environment and often ends up in rivers and oceans,

00:10:31.964 --> 00:10:33.666
which is really bad.

00:10:33.666 --> 00:10:35.067
[Paul] Why is it so bad?

00:10:35.067 --> 00:10:37.803
We don't drink water directly from rivers and oceans.

00:10:37.803 --> 00:10:40.006
We clean it before it
gets into our faucets.

00:10:40.006 --> 00:10:41.674
I learned about that at school.

00:10:41.674 --> 00:10:44.110
[Kate] But fish
don't get it cleaned for them.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:45.444
In the United States,

00:10:45.444 --> 00:10:47.747
the most common
way to be exposed to mercury

00:10:47.747 --> 00:10:49.982
is by eating fish
or shellfish that have

00:10:49.982 --> 00:10:53.652
high levels of mercury.
Come. Let me show you.

00:10:56.555 --> 00:10:59.358
Let's take a closer
look at the environment.

00:10:59.358 --> 00:11:06.565
[Cheerful, playful music begins]

00:11:06.565 --> 00:11:08.501
[Music stops] When
people burn coal for energy,

00:11:08.501 --> 00:11:13.339
the mercury in the coal rocks is released into our environment.

00:11:13.339 --> 00:11:18.177
See? Look how the mercury is getting into the environment.

00:11:18.177 --> 00:11:20.246
Once the mercury
is in the environment,

00:11:20.246 --> 00:11:22.982
it eventually gets
into the soil and water.

00:11:22.982 --> 00:11:25.718
[Paul] But how exactly
does it get into fish?

00:11:25.718 --> 00:11:28.587
[Kate] Let's take a closer
look at the contaminated water.

00:11:35.327 --> 00:11:38.364
Once mercury is in
the water, some microorganisms

00:11:38.364 --> 00:11:41.567
convert it into a very
toxic form of mercury,

00:11:41.567 --> 00:11:44.703
called methylmercury,
which looks like this.

00:11:44.703 --> 00:11:48.140
Then the methylmercury gets into fish by going up the food chain

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:51.243
through a process
called biomagnification.

00:11:51.243 --> 00:11:53.746
First, some tiny
aquatic plants and animals

00:11:53.746 --> 00:11:56.682
absorb the methylmercury
that is in the water.

00:11:56.682 --> 00:11:59.351
Fish and other animals
feed on these tiny aquatic

00:11:59.351 --> 00:12:01.554
plants and animals,
so the methylmercury

00:12:01.554 --> 00:12:03.189
gets passed
on to them.

00:12:03.189 --> 00:12:05.958
Next, bigger fish
eat the smaller fish and

00:12:05.958 --> 00:12:10.029
absorb the methylmercury,
and so on and so forth.

00:12:10.029 --> 00:12:11.931
The higher up
the food chain we go,

00:12:11.931 --> 00:12:14.333
the more mercury
a fish accumulates.

00:12:14.333 --> 00:12:16.202
[Paul] Yuck! Look at
all that methylmercury

00:12:16.202 --> 00:12:18.971
in the tilefish,
sharks, and swordfish!

00:12:18.971 --> 00:12:20.673
[Kate] The longer
these fish have been alive,

00:12:20.673 --> 00:12:23.242
the more time they've
had to eat other fish -

00:12:23.242 --> 00:12:26.045
and the more methylmercury
they have in their bodies.

00:12:26.045 --> 00:12:28.280
Bigger, older fish
that eat other fish

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:31.417
usually have the
highest levels of mercury.

00:12:31.417 --> 00:12:32.952
[Paul] Is it
bad for people?

00:12:32.952 --> 00:12:34.854
[Kate] Well, if people
eat a lot of seafood

00:12:34.854 --> 00:12:37.623
that's high in
mercury, this can be bad!

00:12:40.626 --> 00:12:42.695
Remember, I've said
before that mercury

00:12:42.695 --> 00:12:46.065
is especially bad for
babies and unborn children.

00:12:46.065 --> 00:12:48.701
That's why pregnant women have
to be careful about how much

00:12:48.701 --> 00:12:51.003
mercury-containing
fish they eat.

00:12:51.003 --> 00:12:53.806
[Paul] Oh, no! My sushi!
Are the fish in sushi

00:12:53.806 --> 00:12:55.875
high up in
the food chain?

00:12:55.875 --> 00:12:57.877
Do they accumulate
a lot of mercury?

00:12:57.877 --> 00:12:59.678
Should I stop eating fish?

00:12:59.678 --> 00:13:02.348
[Kate] There are many
benefits to eating fish.

00:13:02.348 --> 00:13:06.085
Also, your mom used salmon and shrimp to make that sushi.

00:13:06.085 --> 00:13:08.354
They usually have
lower levels of mercury.

00:13:08.354 --> 00:13:11.457
If you want to learn more about being safe while eating seafood,

00:13:11.457 --> 00:13:14.360
click on the links
that are on our page.

00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:18.731
[Paul] But how? We're
inside a video - inside a TV!

00:13:18.731 --> 00:13:20.933
[Kate] It's ok
to stop the video,

00:13:20.933 --> 00:13:23.202
or finish watching
and then come back.

00:13:23.202 --> 00:13:25.304
I'm also posting
these links on the webpage

00:13:25.304 --> 00:13:29.542
on our video so you
can read more about mercury.

00:13:29.542 --> 00:13:32.244
[Paul] Wow, I've
learned a lot today.

00:13:32.244 --> 00:13:33.212
[Kate] What
did you learn?

00:13:33.212 --> 00:13:35.681
[Paul] I learned that
mercury is a natural metal.

00:13:35.681 --> 00:13:37.683
People used to
use it in many products,

00:13:37.683 --> 00:13:39.752
but now they use
it less and less.

00:13:39.752 --> 00:13:42.054
Most products we use
at home are safe for us.

00:13:42.054 --> 00:13:44.557
Still, much mercury
ends up in the water and

00:13:44.557 --> 00:13:48.594
accumulates in fish, and that's bad for fish and bad for us.

00:13:48.594 --> 00:13:49.628
[Kate] That's right!

00:13:49.628 --> 00:13:51.564
[Paul] Is there anything
else I should know?

00:13:51.564 --> 00:13:53.933
[Kate] Some cosmetic creams imported from other countries

00:13:53.933 --> 00:13:56.168
could have mercury
at levels much higher

00:13:56.168 --> 00:13:59.238
than allowed for creams manufactured in the U.S.

00:13:59.238 --> 00:14:02.841
Also, some alternative medicine remedies contain mercury,

00:14:02.841 --> 00:14:05.010
and some spiritual and
religious traditions

00:14:05.010 --> 00:14:07.079
use it in
their practices.

00:14:07.079 --> 00:14:08.113
[Paul] That's
interesting.

00:14:08.113 --> 00:14:10.716
Where can I learn
more about all this?

00:14:10.716 --> 00:14:12.918
I know there's a lot of information on the Internet,

00:14:12.918 --> 00:14:14.954
but some things
are difficult to read,and

00:14:14.954 --> 00:14:17.389
sometimes I don't
know who to believe!

00:14:17.389 --> 00:14:18.991
[Kate] You're absolutely right!

00:14:18.991 --> 00:14:21.193
We need good,
reliable information

00:14:21.193 --> 00:14:23.495
that was written for
someone your age.

00:14:23.495 --> 00:14:26.565
This video is part of the National Library of Medicine's

00:14:26.565 --> 00:14:28.834
Environmental
Health Student Portal.

00:14:28.834 --> 00:14:30.369
The portal has
a section on the

00:14:30.369 --> 00:14:32.504
effects of mercury
on human health.

00:14:32.504 --> 00:14:35.007
You can also learn there
about other chemicals in the

00:14:35.007 --> 00:14:38.110
environment and about environmental health.

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:41.313
[Paul] Wow, I'll definitely
check them out. Thank you!

00:14:41.313 --> 00:14:45.417
[Kate] You're very welcome!
Now, let's get you back home!

00:14:47.686 --> 00:14:49.455
[Cat Meowing]

00:14:49.455 --> 00:14:50.556
[Paul] Mom! Hurry!

00:14:50.556 --> 00:14:52.858
There's a TV character
in our living room!

00:14:52.858 --> 00:14:56.629
[Mom] Be there in a second!

00:14:56.629 --> 00:14:58.964
Where is this TV character?

00:14:58.964 --> 00:15:01.233
[Paul] Mom - she was just here!

00:15:01.233 --> 00:15:04.803
[Mom] Sure she was!
Just finish up your sushi!

00:15:20.419 --> 00:15:22.054
This short film was
brought to you by the

00:15:22.054 --> 00:15:23.722
Environmental Health
Student Portal

00:15:23.722 --> 00:15:26.558
of the Division of
Specialized Information Services

00:15:26.558 --> 00:15:29.328
at the U.S. National
Library of Medicine.

00:15:29.328 --> 00:15:32.164
Visit us online at
these great websites!

